Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: qcom: describe ASUS ROG Phone 5 RSC firmware

The existing ASUS board integration avoids the hierarchical PSCI domains
after a recorded OSI transition reset on the kexec boot route. Identify
that integration explicitly while preserving the generic RSC fallback.
Like the existing SC7180/SDM845 cases, permit absence of system-domain
notifications only for the specific compatible. Runtime driver and power
domain properties are unchanged by this binding extension.

Base: 7a5cef0db4795d9d453a12e0f61b5b7634fc4d40 (Linux 7.1.4)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,rpmh-rsc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,rpmh-rsc.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,rpmh-rsc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,rpmh-rsc.yaml
@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@
     oneOf:
       - items:
           - enum:
+              - asus,rog-phone5-rpmh-apps-rsc
               - qcom,sc7180-rpmh-apps-rsc
               - qcom,sdm845-rpmh-apps-rsc
           - const: qcom,rpmh-rsc
@@ -133,14 +134,16 @@
 
 allOf:
   # Some platforms may lack a OSI-mode PSCI implementation, which implies the
-  # system power domain can't provide feedback about entering power collapse
+  # system power domain can't provide feedback about entering power collapse.
+  # ASUS ROG Phone 5 firmware integration also has this limitation after kexec.
   - if:
       not:
         properties:
           compatible:
             contains:
               enum:
+                - asus,rog-phone5-rpmh-apps-rsc
                 - qcom,sc7180-rpmh-apps-rsc
                 - qcom,sdm845-rpmh-apps-rsc
     then:
       required:
